  "mn134:1.3": "Lomasakaṅgiya’s verse speaks of his determination to forge his way through the dense jungle in search of seclusion (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/thag1.27/en/sujato'>Thag 1.27</a>). He is probably also the same monk who appears in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn54.12/en/sujato'>SN 54.12</a>. His name means “hairy-limbs”. ",
  "mn134:2.1": "The god Candana, whose name means “sandalwood”, also appears at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn20/en/sujato#10.5'>DN 20:10.5</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn32/en/sujato#10.4'>DN 32:10.4</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn2.15/en/sujato'>SN 2.15</a>. ",
